{#
  The sheet of payment labels to cut out — see
  Service\PaymentLabelService, which owns every millimetre of this and
  hands the page its stylesheet.

  This template renders no `base.html.twig`, no header and no footer: it
  is the whole of a PDF document's body (Core\Pdf\DocumentPdfService::
  generateBare()), and the labels occupy the sheet up to its margins.
  Anything printed above or beside them would push the ninth row off the
  page.

  **The borders are the cutting lines**, which is why the table is drawn
  even where a row is short: the three cells of a row are always there,
  the empty ones simply carry nothing. A row that drew only two cells
  would leave its third label with no line to cut along.

  **No length is written here.** Widths, heights, paddings and the
  descent of the name's font size all arrive computed from the service —
  a template free to write its own millimetres is a template free to
  disagree with the pagination, and the first symptom of that is a blank
  page between every two sheets.

  The payment details are repeated in text beside the QR, exactly as
  receivable_qr.html.twig does: a code that refuses to scan must never
  leave somebody with no way to pay. The beneficiary is not repeated —
  it is identical on all twenty-seven labels and the IBAN identifies it.
#}
{% for page in pages %}
    <table class="sheet">
        {# batch() is padded with nulls so a short last row still draws its
           three cells: the missing labels have no content, but the lines
           to cut along are exactly as needed. #}
        {% for line in page|batch(columns, null) %}
            <tr>
                {% for label in line %}
                    <td class="label">
                        {% if label %}
                        <div class="inner">
                            {# The QR is FIRST in source order and floated right: a
                               float only shares a line with what follows it. #}
                            <div class="qr">
                                {%- if label.qrDataUri -%}
                                    <img src="{{ label.qrDataUri }}" alt="Code QR de paiement SEPA">
                                {%- endif -%}
                            </div>
                            <div class="text">
                                <p class="name {{ label.nameLines == 1 ? 'one-line' : 'two-lines' }}"
                                   style="font-size: {{ label.nameFontSizePt }}pt;">{{ label.memberName }}</p>
                                <p class="amount">{{ label.amountCents|money_cents }}</p>
                                <p class="pay">
                                    <span class="key">IBAN</span> {{ iban_display }}<br>
                                    <span class="key">Communication</span> {{ label.communication }}
                                </p>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                        {% endif %}
                    </td>
                {% endfor %}
            </tr>
        {% endfor %}
    </table>
    {% if not loop.last %}<div class="page-break"></div>{% endif %}
{% endfor %}
